 "grammar": {
  "title": {
   "ko": "날씨 표현과 예보: It will be / It's going to + 날씨",
   "en": "weather words and forecasts with will and going to"
  },
  "explain": {
   "ko": "일기예보처럼 미래의 날씨는 will + 동사원형이나 be going to로 말합니다. 하늘을 보고 곧 일어날 일을 예상할 때는 It's going to rain.처럼 be going to를 씁니다. 날씨 형용사는 sunny, cloudy, rainy, windy처럼 명사에 -y를 붙여 만듭니다.",
   "en": "Use will + base verb or be going to for forecasts. Use be going to when you can see signs that something is about to happen (It's going to rain). Many weather adjectives are made by adding -y to a noun: sun → sunny, cloud → cloudy, rain → rainy, wind → windy."
  },
  "table": {
   "head": [
    "표현 / Pattern",
    "예 / Example"
   ],
   "rows": [
    [
     "will + be",
     "It will be sunny tomorrow."
    ],
    [
     "be going to",
     "It's going to rain."
    ],
    [
     "현재 / now",
     "It is windy today."
    ],
    [
     "계절 / season",
     "It snows in winter."
    ]
   ]
  },
  "notes": [
   {
    "ko": "예보에는 will, 징후가 보이면 be going to.",
    "en": "will for forecasts; be going to when you see signs."
   },
   {
    "ko": "날씨 -y 형용사: sunny, cloudy, rainy, windy, snowy.",
    "en": "Weather -y adjectives: sunny, cloudy, rainy, windy, snowy."
   },
   {
    "ko": "기온은 degrees로 말합니다: 15 degrees.",
    "en": "Temperatures are in degrees: 15 degrees."
   }
  ],
  "examples": [
   {
    "t": "It will be sunny tomorrow.",
